OBJECTIVE
----------
Quantify orbital chaos during the MW–M31 merger using finite-time Lyapunov exponents (FTLE),
and map how dynamical instability evolves across time, radius, and phase space structure.

SYSTEM STUDIED
--------------
Milky Way–Andromeda merger system:
- Milky Way (MW)
- Andromeda Galaxy (M31)

CORE METHODOLOGY
-----------------
1. Finite-Time Lyapunov Exponents (FTLE)
   - δ(t) = |x_i(t) - x_j(t)| (trajectory separation)
   - ln(δ(t)/δ(0)) used to estimate exponential divergence
   - λ_W(t,i) = (ln δ(t+W) - ln δ(t)) / W
   - Window size: W = 30 snapshots
   - Chaos threshold: λ > 0.02 snap⁻¹

2. Shadow Particle Method
   - Each particle paired with nearest neighbour in initial phase space
   - KD-tree used for efficient nearest-neighbour search
   - Tracks divergence of initially close trajectories

3. Full FTLE Estimation
   - Endpoint finite difference (sliding window)
   - Global regression fit per particle (best λ estimate)

