PHYSICAL INTERPRETATION
-----------------------
- Positive λ indicates exponential orbital divergence → chaotic motion
- Outer halo particles exhibit stronger chaotic behavior
- Chaos onset correlates with merger pericentre passages
- Violent relaxation produces rapid growth in phase-space mixing
- FTLE ridges correspond to transport barriers (tidal structure boundaries)
- Stochastic layer appears around separatrix in (r, v_r) space

KEY RESULTS (QUALITATIVE)
-------------------------
- Clear bifurcation between regular and chaotic orbits
- Strong spike in chaos fraction during merger events
- Outer regions more dynamically unstable than inner halo
- Evidence for inward propagation of chaos after pericentre
- FTLE maps show filamentary coherent structures (LCS)
- Partial correlation between chaos and stripping efficiency

